            <ArticleTitle>[Non-drug prevention of pain in neonatal infants].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>60-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>When treated at a hospital unit, full-term and preterm neonatal infants undergo a large number of manipulations and procedures, most of them are rather painful; anesthesia is used inadequately frequently. Pain prevention during procedures is able to reduce a baby's discomfort and to improve his/her tolerance of medical manipulations and care procedures.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
